Z||000000||DJRice||08-13-99||07:19 AM||||I was just thumbing through some of the posts on the Tech Disscussion and decided to click on your profile.<p>Greetings to a fellow Boeing Employee.  I am working EELV at Kennedy Space Center, FL.<p>I thought that was pretty interesting.
Z||000001||BN Boomer||08-13-99||01:23 PM||||I worked as an assembly mechanic at Boeing's Everett plant for 6 1/2 years before taking a voluntary layoff and going to work for Burlington Northern railroad 5 years ago. I came back for a month when I was called back in 97 but found I really didn't care for working by bells and whistles or under constant supervision, it almost felt like returning to school. My wife has been there for 13 years now. The primary reason I left was because I no longer felt too comfortable having all our financial eggs in the Boeing basket given their cyclical layoffs and outsourcing. My father in-law worked for them in engineering, quality control, and supervision for 33 years, mostly in the defense division and finally as a third level manager in the 777 division, before taking the "Golden Handshake" retirement package back in 95. Now he works for the FAA as an inspector at the Everett plant.
Z||000002||lowCG||08-13-99||03:52 PM||||I'm actually in the laid off mode,really liked what I did at Boeing,but,coming from a model-maker/design background,I feel that I need to pursue this.Met a lot of very interesting people,and enjoyed the interaction while working as a planner.<br>Trying to get something together for a possible job opening in Detroit for a large auto company,just got back from a meeting with the guy who designed the '69 Mach One.<br>BN,do you know of a guy named Reuf Kapetonovic,who used to work for BNRR?<br>FAA gig sounds pretty neat.<br>DJ,what do you do at Kennedy,if I may ask?
Z||000003||DJRice||08-16-99||06:54 AM||||I am designing the CCTV and Video Distribution system for Launch Complex 37.  It is being rebuilt to launch the Delta IV rocket.<p>The opportunity to work on a new rocket is very interesting, but right now there is a whole lot of paper pushing going on here.<p>Boeing is working on a restructuring plan that is supposed to solve the layoff problems.  They are trying to form a "matrix organization" that is supposed to "match talent with need"<p>Who knows what will happen then....
Z||000004||theogre||08-16-99||08:28 AM||||guys, some of what you are talking about is likely considered proprietary data by Boeing. There have been several law suites by companies against employees for talking about such stuff in public chat areas, some are still pending, inlcuding a large against 10-20 people who chatted in an AOL forum.<p>It's not as likely that this forum is watched like AOL is, but I'd hate to see you all end up in crap over stupid nonsense. I know it sounds paranoid, but that's the way business and the legal system are these days.
